                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Devilish, demonic, ass-cancer, buggy-ass game. Within the first few hours, you get to see a man suck off Satan. Also, gay seggs. Peak gameplay.\n\n**Lucius 2: Electric Boogaloo** is the panned sequel to the panned cult classic Lucius 1.\n\nBoth are terrible games, just in two completely different ways.\n\nThis game is mostly (I think) functional. It crashed twice in five hours, which, by Bethesda standards, is fantastic. I only got lost once, in the penultimate level, because, for some reason, a door that told me to find some keys was actually opened by a lever.\n\nIn Lucius 2, Fellatio Detective is helping you for some reason, even though he knows you're the devilspawn and that you, apparently inspired by Caim's antics, competitively obliterated your entire family.\n\nWhy does a man who knows you did all of that still help you, you ask? Fuck if I know. They change his motivations from game to game. Next time around, he'll probably try to talk you out of your antics.\n\nThis is kinda like a Hitman game if the enemy AI were somehow even more lobotomized. YOU CAN POISON SHIT and throw it at people in plain sight, and they'll straight-up eat that poisoned goyslop and die. And no one will suspect you. You can explode people with chemicals, pressure valves, and whatnot, and no one will give a single flying fuck.\n\nI possessed a sussy redneck who kept decapitated heads in his fridge and had him chop 20 people to death.\n\nI accidentally blew up five people with a fucking table saw because the physics are completely broken.\n\nThis game is not good. I loved it. Don't try to understand it. You won't.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1793389081,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1793389081,
                        "voted_up": true,
